{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>I dwell with cunning</b> — it lacks a bet, like שכן ארץ. The meaning: that cunning requires wisdom, for it cannot succeed without it." "<b>And knowledge of designs I find</b> — and knowledge of the designs of those who seek him I find and reach the end of their intention. And it is possible to interpret: I, Wisdom, am acquainted with and know all cunning, as though I dwell within it, and I also descend to the depth of the knowledge of every design; and since knowledge is what is found after wisdom and understanding, he said the word אמצא. The meaning: that no design is beyond the reach of wisdom."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:25.281831522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}